# Complete adapter diagnostics (issue 123)

The adapter runner now retains original stdout and stderr bytes in persistent,
run-owned files. Each session records paths, byte counts, SHA-256 hashes, command,
source binding, native exit status, capture failures and controlled interruption.
The final record is written after the child closes and its streams drain. An
unfinished record explicitly identifies a checkpoint; it does not claim complete
capture. Console text is labelled as a decoded display of the authoritative raw
files. Nonprotocol stdout is no longer clipped, and native failure messages no
longer discard middle stderr lines.

Implementation base: `4f06a71180e90bc90b5fb754b3d7f3d902a94e45`.
The original adapter and runner files matched reference
`420ce6869677b9b7a94a02f4d5c79ccc8dcbdf86` exactly. No Area 6 release instrument
was imported or replaced.

