## Fixture correction and cleanup

An initial controlled fixture left stdin open after ending its protocol loop.
Its verified owned Node child, PID 50044, was terminated after checking its full
command and parent. That failed run is excluded from the passing evidence. The
fixture now destroys its stdin after the loop; the passing tests independently
check that their owned children are gone. No unrelated process was stopped.

Tests remove their own temporary session directories after checking persistence
and shutdown. Run-owned evidence under `.runtime/adapter123` is retained. Before
this report, the seven payload paths contained 89,640 bytes versus 68,019 tracked
bytes before the patch: 21,621 net source bytes added, zero existing source bytes
deleted as cleanup. These are file-content counts, not allocated disk usage.

