## Independent review correction: final manifest publication

Review commit `fdf5a602e8cc6b42a0d70e80e46c68ae3b9eaefa` exposed a
remaining failure in the first repair, `ed1f2e1899562b60920c994eaa439d59e9fd672d`.
An existing owned `diagnostics.json.next` file causes the final publication to
throw EEXIST. Previously, `update` had already changed the live state to complete,
so the runner could copy that claim while the disk manifest remained an older
checkpoint. This required another review cycle and is corrected here.

`update` now publishes a candidate before accepting its successful state. If
publication fails, its getter exposes `capture-failed`, `streams_complete:false`,
the real capture error and structured `manifest_publication_error`. The existing
checkpoint and raw bytes remain intact; close still rejects. Only the diagnostic
journal, the independent regression test and this report change in this followup.

The independent test is included unchanged: Git blob
`2bf958806e69b62e97f6266cab0a29390dca974c`. It fails against the original
`ed1f2e189` journal and adapter with the expected `true !== false` assertion.
The same test and all 11 owner controls pass after repair. Raw outputs:

- `.runtime/adapter123/finalization-before.tap`, SHA-256
  `6b610b0f896c37ca1c1150e5a220796d5efc8c5c9d6827f83cff7a3781f37d39`.
- `.runtime/adapter123/finalization-after.tap`, SHA-256
  `ba08d281ef296ac7b198abfdc6153458665efe0d3c4a72e156a5a8f57bbbbbd0c`.

The tests confirm owned-child shutdown even when final publication fails. The
baseline comparison uses small explicitly named source copies under `.runtime`,
retained with its evidence; it is not a second checkout or runnable release.

The final combined run passed 77 tests in 13 suites, zero failures,
cancellations or skips. It adds the independent test to the original combined
command above. Raw output `.runtime/adapter123/finalization-regression.tap` has
SHA-256 `496ec2622c746eb72cd08c084f4f4a4706355091da67fd503553942393993fb7`.
TypeScript, whitespace and the two-file platform scan passed. A read-only
